WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:04.470
Three-headed metal dragons and an all-out
assault on Hong Kong!

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:08.521
These high-octane robo-brawls transform the
series into something great.

00:00:08.669 --> 00:00:12.430
The first scene of Transformer action in the
series is also one of the best.

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:18.060
It has to be — it's the moment in 2007's
"Transformers" that the Decepticons decide

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.500
the importance of finding the All-Spark outweighs
the costs of remaining hidden.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.789
It's also the first time that humans become
aware of robots in disguise among us.

00:00:26.789 --> 00:00:29.208
“You can call us autobots for short.”

00:00:29.208 --> 00:00:30.208
“Autobots.”

00:00:30.208 --> 00:00:32.029
“What’s crackin’, little b–tches?”

00:00:32.029 --> 00:00:36.570
What starts out as a stressful but believably
human encounter between the U.S. military

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:41.590
and an unidentified helicopter quickly turns
into a huge battle between the service members

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:45.020
of a Qatar base and the Decepticon Blackout.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:50.000
There's heavy gunfire, rockets, and an alien
concussion weapon that sends a shockwave through

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.526
the entire base, smashing glass and sending
soldiers flying.

00:00:54.526 --> 00:00:59.280
"Revenge of the Fallen" introduces a number
of new Autobots and Decepticons over the course

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:02.770
of the movie, and this major battle shows
them go head to head with one another.

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:07.130
But what's most exciting about this action
sequence is the smaller-scale battle within

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:11.280
a battle that Bumblebee has with Decepticons
Rampage and Ravage.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:16.190
Bumblebee is protecting Shia LaBeouf's Sam,
Megan Fox's Mikaela, and Sam's parents from

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:17.750
an attack by Rampage.

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:22.270
Meanwhile, Ravage — who's taken the form
of a big cat — attempts a sneak attack.

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:26.705
But Bumblebee is too quick and literally rips
the smaller robot's spine out.

00:01:26.705 --> 00:01:31.047
"Revenge of the Fallen" opens with NEST and
the Autobots traveling to Shanghai to find

00:01:31.047 --> 00:01:32.631
Decepticons hiding out on Earth.

00:01:32.631 --> 00:01:38.320
Demolisher, a giant Transformer, comes to
life and immediately begins to destroy everything

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:39.380
it can reach.

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:44.742
Optimus Prime is dropped from a carrier plane
and attacks just as Demolisher destroys an overpass.

00:01:44.742 --> 00:01:50.220
Optimus easily brings down the giant Decepticon,
but its destructive run has already taken

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:56.250
a toll on the city, while offering fans one
of the most exciting action scenes in the franchise.

00:01:56.379 --> 00:02:00.520
This sequence starts off on the top floor
of a skyscraper — one being toppled by the

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.330
invading Decepticons.

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:06.530
Unfortunately, our human heroes are at the
very top, and the real excitement comes when

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:09.330
they decide it's time to escape from an armed
robot.

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:13.530
They leap out of the windows of the leaning
skyscraper and begin to slide down the edge

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:15.580
of the building at breakneck speed.

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:19.360
Tyrese Gibson's Sergeant Epps has the idea
to shoot out the glass of the windows the

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:23.950
heroes are sliding down so that they can re-enter
the building, but when they fall back inside,

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:27.980
they just start sliding across the floor in
the opposite direction as the building's lean

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:30.160
turns more into a full-on fall.

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:34.540
The characters desperately grab at whatever
is around, all while avoiding falling office

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:38.740
objects, and while most survive, some plummet
to their death.

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:42.980
This "Revenge of the Fallen" scene begins
when a group of trucks and construction vehicles

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:48.120
converge on a sandpit, with human characters
Simmons and Leo watching nervously.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:53.160
The multiple vehicles begin to transform,
with these Decepticons, known as the "Constructicons,"

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:55.599
beginning to form one gigantic Transformer.

00:02:55.599 --> 00:03:00.030
The kaiju-sized Devastator doesn't even allow
Simmons and Leo to be scared of how big it

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:02.636
is before it begins its first attack.

00:03:02.636 --> 00:03:05.840
"Mean robot suck!"

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:10.030
It creates an extremely powerful vacuum in
its mouth that draws sand from the desert

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:13.320
and every nearby vehicle into its gaping maw.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:17.510
And when the cars enter its mouth, they're
crushed and explode out of Devastator's back

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:19.698
in a plume of fire and smoke.

00:03:19.808 --> 00:03:23.959
Towards the end of "Transformer's" climactic
battle in Mission City, Bumblebee has been

00:03:23.959 --> 00:03:26.140
seriously wounded and has lost his legs.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:30.610
But Mikaela is quick to act and hooks his
torso up to a tow truck and gets them both

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.129
to safety in an alley.

00:03:32.129 --> 00:03:36.910
But that safety only lasts a moment as Mikaela
kicks the tow truck into high gear and speeds

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:41.968
back out into the fray, only stopping for
a quick moment to turn back to Bumblebee and say:

00:03:41.968 --> 00:03:46.790
"I'll drive, you shoot!"

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:50.810
It's one of the best lines in the franchise,
and it leads into one of the best human-Transformer

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:52.830
action moments in all of the movies.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:57.300
Mikaela drives backwards so that Bumblebee
can face his enemies, and together, the two

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:00.540
rush a Decepticon the human soldiers are unable
to bring down.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:05.239
As they drive, Bumblebee unloads almost the
entire arsenal of his weapons.

00:04:05.239 --> 00:04:09.610
But more than that, he has to move the destroyed
cars in the street out of their way, leading

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:13.670
to some classic Michael Bay car flips that
are such a small part of the larger action

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:15.788
here they just feel like grace notes.

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:21.040
In "Age of Extinction," entrepreneur Stanley
Tucci's Joshua Joyce discovers "transformium"

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.349
can be programmed.

00:04:22.349 --> 00:04:26.710
Not only that, after mapping its genome, it
can be given instruction by humans.

00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:31.279
The first action scene we get to see with
the newly human-programmed Transformers, Galvatron

00:04:31.279 --> 00:04:33.789
and Stinger, is a massive highway chase.

00:04:33.789 --> 00:04:38.900
Galvatron and Stinger are sent after the Autobots
by Joyce and his company, but they soon begin

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:43.639
to act on their own and destroy cars driven
by innocent civilians for fun while engaging

00:04:43.639 --> 00:04:44.839
the Autobots.

00:04:44.839 --> 00:04:49.910
But the real excitement is the way the transformium
allows these new robots to transform and re-form.

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:54.000
Their transformations are fluid, almost as
if they turn into a metallic liquid made up

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.490
of tiny shards between vehicle and robot form.

00:04:56.490 --> 00:05:01.710
When Bumblebee fires a series of shots that
perfectly connect with Galvatron, the transformium

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:07.254
robot explodes into bits of metal before simply
reforming as a vehicle behind Bumblebee.

00:05:07.254 --> 00:05:11.830
Early in "The Last Knight," Mark Wahlberg's
Cade Yeager searches the ruins of the aftermath

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:17.469
of the battle of Chicago for any Autobot survivors
and is attacked by the newly formed Transformers

00:05:17.469 --> 00:05:19.870
Reaction Force, aka TRF.

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:23.330
They have him surrounded, and things don't
look good.

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:27.930
But Bumblebee comes rushing onto the scene
in car form, leaps over a hail of bullet fire

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:31.780
from the TRF members, transforms ... and falls
apart.

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:35.560
He lands on the ground in the middle of the
TRF soldiers in several pieces.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:39.779
But it only takes a second before he goes
on the offensive with those disparate limbs,

00:05:39.779 --> 00:05:44.729
almost every single part of his disarticulated
body attacking individually at the same time.

00:05:44.729 --> 00:05:47.050
He begins to reassemble all the while.

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:51.497
It's a great sequence that adds a new attack
option for one of the most beloved Autobots.

00:05:51.497 --> 00:05:56.167
“Bumblebee, we only met when I was a little
boy in short pants.

00:05:56.167 --> 00:05:58.652
I must’ve been that tall, maybe taller.”

00:05:58.652 --> 00:06:04.099
In "Age of Extinction," as a battle rages
in Hong Kong, Optimus decides that they need reinforcements.

00:06:04.099 --> 00:06:08.590
He goes to the ship that contains some legendary
warriors, the Dinobots, and wakes them up

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:11.259
in hopes that they will join the fight for
the Autobots.

00:06:11.259 --> 00:06:15.620
But they don't immediately jump at the chance
to serve as allies, and instead, Optimus takes

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:19.499
them on, proving that he can beat them and
is a leader worthy of their allegiance.

00:06:19.499 --> 00:06:24.569
It's an incredible fight scene, not only because
we get to finally see the Dinobots in action

00:06:24.569 --> 00:06:29.039
in both dinosaur and robot form but also because
their scale is astounding.

00:06:29.039 --> 00:06:35.611
Optimus, a very large robot by most measurements,
is a fraction of the size of these legendary Transformers.

00:06:35.611 --> 00:06:40.279
After the Hong Kong battle turns the Autobots'
way, there's a brief moment for celebration,

00:06:40.279 --> 00:06:42.159
but then Lockdown arrives.

00:06:42.159 --> 00:06:46.869
The bounty hunter's massive ship opens a strange
looking weapon that begins to draw all metal

00:06:46.869 --> 00:06:48.509
objects towards it.

00:06:48.509 --> 00:06:52.919
But it's not just small metal objects — it's
literally everything, from the beams within

00:06:52.919 --> 00:06:55.669
buildings to entire cars and boats.

00:06:55.669 --> 00:07:00.219
The giant magnet leads to a widespread destruction
that's only made worse when the heroes realize

00:07:00.219 --> 00:07:03.080
that it's not just picking up all the metal
in the city.

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:07.499
It's alternating between lifting and dropping
these objects, causing massive shipping boats

00:07:07.499 --> 00:07:09.099
to rain from the sky.

00:07:09.099 --> 00:07:13.759
During all this chaos, the movie focuses on
our human heroes who are in a car, attempting

00:07:13.759 --> 00:07:15.969
to not get sucked up into the magnet.

00:07:15.969 --> 00:07:20.259
It's a sort of chase sequence, but instead
of being chased by another vehicle or even

00:07:20.259 --> 00:07:25.000
a Transformer, our lead characters are trying
to escape death and destruction by magnet.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:28.419
The "Transformers" franchise isn't known for
its emotional heft.

00:07:28.419 --> 00:07:32.979
But sometimes, those over-the-top action scenes
can hit you in the feels, such as the fight

00:07:32.979 --> 00:07:36.229
between Nemesis Prime and Bumblebee in "The
Last Knight."

00:07:36.229 --> 00:07:40.939
Optimus has been brainwashed by the powerful
Transformer Quintessa and renamed Nemesis

00:07:40.939 --> 00:07:42.539
Prime as he serves her wishes.

00:07:42.539 --> 00:07:47.659
At one point, Bumblebee pursues his former
leader and engages him in a fight on a resurfacing

00:07:47.659 --> 00:07:49.610
ship in the middle of the ocean.

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:54.389
The fight between Bumblebee and Nemesis is
simultaneously thrilling and heartbreaking,

00:07:54.389 --> 00:07:58.495
as we know these two have great love for one
another and shouldn't be set against each other.

00:07:58.495 --> 00:08:03.419
Their fight is brutal, and the sequence is
only made more exciting and emotionally difficult

00:08:03.419 --> 00:08:07.639
to watch as Cade places himself in the middle
of the fight and attempts to draw out the

00:08:07.639 --> 00:08:11.039
real Optimus, who would never fight his old
friend.

00:08:11.039 --> 00:08:12.722
"I am bumblebee.

00:08:12.722 --> 00:08:14.587
Your oldest friend."

00:08:14.587 --> 00:08:19.349
After our heroes make that skyscraper jump
in "Dark of the Moon," Decepticon Shockwave

00:08:19.349 --> 00:08:22.520
notices that there are still survivors in
the skyscraper.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:26.639
So he calls on his trusted enforcer Driller
to take down the rest of the building.

00:08:26.639 --> 00:08:31.979
Driller is a huge snake-like Decepticon with
one massive cylindrical central body and several

00:08:31.979 --> 00:08:35.650
tendrils that it uses to break things apart
in its path.

00:08:35.650 --> 00:08:38.810
Driller immediately gets to work tearing through
the lower levels of the building.

00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:42.700
It looks as if it's swimming like a flying
fish, coming up and down through the glass

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:43.810
of the building.

00:08:43.810 --> 00:08:47.900
But soon it begins to change its approach
and starts to ensnare the building in a massive

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:51.300
constriction at the point where it was already
beginning to lean.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:55.340
The constriction breaks the final hold of
the building and brings it perpendicular with

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:58.927
itself before Driller makes a final attack
on the building.

00:08:58.927 --> 00:09:03.850
After Cemetery Wind attacks Cade's family
farm while searching for Optimus, Cade, his

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:08.760
daughter Tess, their friend Lucas, and Tess'
secret boyfriend, Shane, try to escape while

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:11.280
being pursued by military-grade vehicles.

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:16.610
The chase takes them through cornfields, backyards,
a small nearby town, and finally an abandoned

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:18.640
factory lot at extreme speeds.

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:23.050
Along with the requisite car flips and a thrilling
high-speed leap from an upper story of the

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:27.510
factory onto a ramp below, the final moments
of the chase are paralleled by a fight between

00:09:27.510 --> 00:09:29.620
Optimus Prime and Lockdown.

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:33.750
The fight takes them over the rooftops of
the factory lot and includes Optimus making

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:37.030
use of a crane to ensnare and hang Lockdown.

00:09:37.030 --> 00:09:41.110
But perhaps the most visually exciting moment
comes when Optimus blocks our human heroes

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:45.440
from their pursuers by essentially barrel-rolling
over the Cemetery Wind cars.

00:09:45.928 --> 00:09:50.610
"The Last Knight" opens with a medieval battle
that we learn Transformers assisted in, and

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:54.360
the story centers on finding a wizard's staff
so that the world can be saved.

00:09:54.360 --> 00:10:03.235
“Let those who exist long after us know,
that this, was our finest hour.”

00:10:03.235 --> 00:10:07.200
Perhaps the most exciting part of the more
fantasy-leaning "Last Knight," visually at

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:09.940
least, is the inclusion of Dragonstorm.

00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:14.060
Dragonstorm is a huge three-headed metal dragon
formed by the combining of the Knights of

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:16.890
Iacon, guardian knights of the staff of Merlin.

00:10:16.890 --> 00:10:20.970
The knights form into this glorious dragon
form in the finale of the "The Last Knight"

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:26.190
to participate in the aerial battle that takes
place over, under, and between the colliding

00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:28.440
Cybertron and Earth planets.

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:33.110
The fight between Optimus Prime, Sentinel
Prime, and Megatron in the final moments of

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:36.970
"Dark of the Moon" remains the most brutal
fight in the entire series.

00:10:36.970 --> 00:10:41.160
The sequence begins with a thrilling fight
between Optimus and Sentinel, who's betrayed

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:44.520
his Autobot comrades to work with the Decepticons.

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:48.550
But just when things look most bleak for Optimus
and Sentinel is about to strike a killing

00:10:48.550 --> 00:10:51.760
blow, Megatron opens fire on Sentinel.

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:56.930
As Megatron beats Sentinel, Optimus returns
to his feet, and when Megatron suggests a

00:10:56.930 --> 00:11:02.030
truce, Optimus rips his head and spinal cord
from the rest of his body using his ax.

00:11:02.030 --> 00:11:07.630
As Megatron's parts disconnect, there's a
spray of sparks and fluid that's essentially Transformer blood.

00:11:07.630 --> 00:11:13.250
But that's not the end of the scene, as Optimus
then turns his attention to Sentinel and quite

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:17.339
literally kills him execution style with a
shotgun blast to the head.

